  "content": {
    "id": "p39-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "The population of a country is doubling every 30 years, and was $3\\,000\\,000$ at the last census.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p39-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Explain why the population $P$ after another $n$ years is $P=3\\,000\\,000\\times2^{n/30}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "There are $\\frac{n}{30}$ thirty-year intervals in $n$ years, and the population doubles in each interval.",
          "worked": "The initial population is $3\\,000\\,000$. There are $\\frac{n}{30}$ doubling periods in $n$ years, so the initial population is multiplied by $2^{n/30}$:\n\n$$P=3\\,000\\,000\\times2^{n/30}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q3-b",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the population (nearest million) after:",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p39-q3-b-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "90 years",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$24\\,000\\,000$ people.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P&=3\\,000\\,000\\times2^{90/30}\\\\P&=3\\,000\\,000\\times8\\\\P&=24\\,000\\,000.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe population is $24\\,000\\,000$ people.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 36
          },
          {
            "id": "p39-q3-b-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "100 years.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$30\\,000\\,000$ people.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P&=3\\,000\\,000\\times2^{100/30}\\\\P&=3\\,000\\,000\\times2^{10/3}\\\\P&\\approx30\\,238\\,105.\\end{align*}$$\n\nTo the nearest million, the population is $30\\,000\\,000$ people.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 36
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q3-c",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "By substituting into the equation, find (nearest year) when the population will be:",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p39-q3-c-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "$48\\,000\\,000$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "120 years after the last census.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}48\\,000\\,000&=3\\,000\\,000\\times2^{n/30}\\\\2^{n/30}&=16\\\\\\frac{n}{30}&=\\log_2 16\\\\\\frac{n}{30}&=4\\\\n&=120.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe population reaches $48\\,000\\,000$ after 120 years.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 54
          },
          {
            "id": "p39-q3-c-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "$60\\,000\\,000$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "130 years after the last census.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}60\\,000\\,000&=3\\,000\\,000\\times2^{n/30}\\\\2^{n/30}&=20\\\\\\frac{n}{30}&=\\log_2 20\\\\n&=30\\frac{\\log_{10}20}{\\log_{10}2}\\\\n&\\approx129.6578.\\end{align*}$$\n\nTo the nearest year, the population reaches $60\\,000\\,000$ after 130 years.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 54
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
